Weston: retain the view-list assertion only when the surface has views.

Backport of upstream f3e30e4692f02f3d6183a3c88b5ac59c9a8b610a to 15.0.1.
https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/wayland/weston/-/commit/f3e30e4692f02f3d6183a3c88b5ac59c9a8b610a
Mirror: https://github.com/wayland-mirror/weston/commit/f3e30e4692f02f3d6183a3c88b5ac59c9a8b610a
Author: Derek Foreman <derek.foreman@collabora.com>

The headless Wayland shard hit surface-state.c:282 while restoring native
windows. With no views, weston_view_geometry_dirty is never called and need
not set view_list_needs_rebuild. Keep the assertion for surfaces with views.
Regression: src/tests/native/gui/shell/probes/linux/UnmappedSubsurface.c.

--- a/libweston/surface-state.c
+++ b/libweston/surface-state.c
@@ -282 +282,2 @@ weston_surface_apply_subsurface_order(struct weston_surface *surface)
-	weston_assert_true(comp, comp->view_list_needs_rebuild);
+	if (!wl_list_empty(&surface->views))
+		weston_assert_true(comp, comp->view_list_needs_rebuild);
